factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 6 problems
  The tamil_headline says the wall is 'near' (அருகே) the old court and calls it 'சுவர்', but the article says the power pole was relocated; the headline's added 'விபத்து ஏற்படுத்திய' describes the pole as causing accidents, which the article does not state directly (it says the road had frequent accidents, not that the pole caused them).
  The reel_script says the pole was 'ஆபத்தாக நின்ற' on the road and the slides say the pole 'ஆபத்தான நிலையில்' was beside the road; the article says it was 'சாலையை ஒட்டியே ஆபத்தான நிலையில்', so this is consistent, but the reel_script states the wall was demolished 'after' the pole became dangerous, and it mixes the timeline of the wall demolition arrangement with the pole's status.
  The reel_script says the minister 'உத்தரவிட்டார்' to remove the pole 'உடனடியாக' citing the temple festival; the article attributes the festival reason and disaster-management rule directly to the minister's speech, which is fine, but the reel_script omits that the order was given to electricity board officials under disaster management rules, which is an important cause/detail.
  The reel_script says the pole was 'வேறிடத்திற்கு மாற்றப்பட்டுள்ளது' and then that the minister inspected the work 'நேற்று'; the caption's date line gives 'நவம்பர் 5, 2026' which is the posting date and is acceptable, but the caption's event line states the inspection was 'நேற்று' without a matching date in the article, which is relative and fine.
  The slides_spec line 'போக்குவரத்து இடையூறு குறைய வாய்ப்பு' (chance of reduced traffic obstruction) is an inferred outcome not stated in the article.
  The caption says 'கோவில் திருவிழா நேரத்தில் இந்தச் சாலையில் போக்குவரத்து கவனமாக இருங்கள்', a public advisory that the article does not contain, so it is an invented detail.
